== Overview ==
Unlike many joke languages that are intentionally unusable or limited to stack machines, WibuScript is Turing-complete, feature-rich, and compiles directly to modern JavaScript. It includes a complete Lexer, Parser (AST generator), Transpiler, and interactive REPL, with runtime support for standard data structures, asynchronous operations, file I/O, error handling, and object-oriented programming.

WibuScript features four canonical dialects with 100% syntactic and semantic parity. A program written in any dialect executes with identical behavior, and code written across different dialects can even be mixed within the same source file.

== Dialects ==
The four official dialects of WibuScript are:
# '''Jepang Murni (Pure Japanese)''': Romanized Japanese keywords providing a formal anime/manga atmosphere.
# '''Jepang Singkat (Short Japanese)''': Compact, abbreviated keywords optimized for concise typing and competitive coding.
# '''Wibu Absurd (Absurd Weeb)''': Highly expressive dialect based on contemporary Indonesian anime community slang and otaku expressions.
# '''Meme Rongawi (Rongawi Meme)''': Humorous and satirical dialect drawing from Indonesian surreal internet humor and Rongawi subculture.

