== Examples ==

=== [[Hello, world!]] ===
All four dialects support printing output to standard output:

; Pure Japanese
<pre>
mite("Konnichiwa Sekai!")
</pre>

; Short Japanese
<pre>
mi("Konnichiwa Sekai!")
</pre>

; Absurd Weeb
<pre>
iuYo("Halo Dunia Wibu!")
</pre>

; Meme Rongawi
<pre>
salamkenal("Sugeng Rawuh ing Donya Rongawi!")
</pre>

=== [[Truth-machine]] ===
A standard esolang benchmark Truth-machine implementation:

; Pure Japanese
<pre>
kore inputVal = 1

moshi (inputVal == 0) {
  mite(0)
} soretomo (inputVal == 1) {
  zutto (hontou) {
    mite(1)
  }
}
</pre>

; Absurd Weeb
<pre>
iniDesu inputVal = 1

moShiKalo (inputVal == 0) {
  iuYo(0)
} soredemoNe (inputVal == 1) {
  zuttoLoop (hontouNi) {
    iuYo(1)
  }
}
</pre>

=== FizzBuzz ===
FizzBuzz implemented in Pure Japanese:
<pre>
kore i = 1
zutto (i <= 100) {
  moshi (i % 15 == 0) {
    mite("FizzBuzz")
  } soretomo (i % 3 == 0) {
    mite("Fizz")
  } soretomo (i % 5 == 0) {
    mite("Buzz")
  } hoka {
    mite(i)
  }
  i = i + 1
}
</pre>

=== Object-Oriented Programming ===
Demonstrating classes, constructors, methods, and inheritance:
<pre>
sekte Pendekar {
  tanjou(nama, klan) {
    jibun.nama = nama
    jibun.klan = klan
    jibun.chakra = 100
  }

  status() {
    kaesu "[Pendekar: " + jibun.nama + " | Klan: " + jibun.klan + "]"
  }

  latihan(jam) {
    jibun.chakra = jibun.chakra + (jam * 10)
    mite(jibun.nama + " berlatih. Chakra: " + jibun.chakra)
  }
}

sekte Kage keishou Pendekar {
  tanjou(nama, klan, gelar) {
    jibun.nama = nama
    jibun.klan = klan
    jibun.chakra = 500
    jibun.gelar = gelar
  }

  jurusPemberantas() {
    jibun.chakra = jibun.chakra - 50
    mite(jibun.gelar + " " + jibun.nama + " Rasengan! Chakra: " + jibun.chakra)
  }
}

kore naruto = atarashii Kage("Naruto", "Uzumaki", "Hokage")
mite(naruto.status())
naruto.jurusPemberantas()
naruto.latihan(2)
</pre>

== Computational Class ==
WibuScript is [[Turing complete]]. It provides arbitrary mutable variables, arithmetic operations, conditional branching, recursion, unbounded while-loops, dynamic arrays, and first-class functions. Any program expressible in JavaScript can be directly modeled and executed in WibuScript.

